 data; on a premium site you pay with money.</p>\n<p>Understanding which currency you are spending — and whether the exchange is fair — is the whole decision.</p></div>\n<nav class=\"toc\" aria-label=\"Table of contents\"><p class=\"toc-h\">Contents</p><ul><li><a href=\"#what-free-actually-costs-1\">What free actually costs</a></li><li><a href=\"#what-premium-actually-buys-2\">What premium actually buys</a></li><li><a href=\"#the-trap-in-the-middle-3\">The trap in the middle</a></li><li><a href=\"#how-we-note-it-on-dark-ero-4\">How we note it on Dark-Ero</a></li><li><a href=\"#more-guides-guides-5\">More Guides guides</a></li></ul></nav>\n<div class=\"article-meta\"><span>Dark-Ero editorial</span><span>2026-09-30</span></div>\n<article class=\"prose\">\n    <p style=\"font-size:18px;color:var(--text)\">The real trade is not price against no-price. It is your attention against your money.</p>\n    <p>Every adult site is free to someone. On an ad-supported site you pay with attention and data; on a premium site you pay with money.</p>\n    <p>Understanding which currency you are spending — and whether the exchange is fair — is the whole decision.</p><h2 id=\"what-free-actually-costs-1\">What free actually costs</h2><p>Free sites monetise through advertising, and adult advertising is among the most aggressive on the web. The cost shows up as pop-ups, autoplay, redirects, and tracking that follows you across sites.</p>\n    <p>For casual browsing this is a fair trade. For anything you care about keeping private, it is not.</p><h2 id=\"what-premium-actually-buys-2\">What premium actually buys</h2><p>A premium subscription buys three things: no advertising, higher quality, and — on the better sites — some assurance that performers were paid and consented. That last point is worth more than it looks.</p>\n    <p>The gap between a reputable paid studio and an anonymous free aggregator is not just resolution.</p><h2 id=\"the-trap-in-the-middle-3\">The trap in the middle</h2><p>The dangerous zone is the discounted trial. A site advertises a low first-month price, then rebills at three or four times that, and buries the cancellation flow.</p>\n    <p>This is the single most common complaint about paid adult sites, and it is entirely avoidable.</p><div class=\"callout\"><p>Before you enter a card on any paid site, find the cancellation page first. If you can&#x27;t find it in under a minute, that is the review — don&#x27;t subscribe.</p></div><h2 id=\"how-we-note-it-on-dark-ero-4\">How we note it on Dark-Ero</h2><p>Every premium entry records the real renewal price, not the trial price, and a note on how hard cancellation is. That is the information the sites themselves work hardest to hide, so it is the information we work hardest to surface.</p>\n    <div class=\"callout safe\"><p>Browsing this topic? See the <a href=\"/category/premium/\">Premium</a> section of the directory for hand-checked sites.</p></div>\n    <hr class=\"divider\" style=\"margin:34px 0\">\n    <p style=\"font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)\">This guide is general information, not legal or security advice. Laws on adult content vary by country — check what applies where you live.</p>\n  </article>\n  <div style=\"display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:30px 0\"><a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/blog/how-to-tell-a-real-adult-site-from-a-malware-trap/\">← How to tell a real adult site from…</a><a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/blog/why-free-onlyfans-links-are-almost-always-a-scam/\">Why &#x27;free OnlyFans&#x27; links are almo… →</a></div>\n  <section class=\"section\" style=\"padding-top:0\">\n    <div class=\"section-head\"><h2 id=\"more-guides-guides-5\">More Guides guides</h2><a href=\"/blog/topic/guides/\">All →</a></div>\n    <div class=\"post-list\"><article class=\"post-card\">\n      <div class=\"tagline\"><a href=\"/blog/topic/guides/\" style=\"color:inherit\">Guides</a></div>\n      <h3><a href=\"/blog/reading-cam-site-pricing-before-it-reads-your-wallet/\">Reading cam site pricing before it reads your wallet</a></h3>\n      <p>Tokens, tips and private shows are designed to obscure the real cost. Here is how to see through it.</p>\n      <a class=\"more\" href=\"/blog/reading-cam-site-pricing-before-it-reads-your-wallet/\">Read guide →</a>\n    </article><article class=\"post-card\">\n      <div class=\"tagline\"><a href=\"/blog/topic/guides/\" style=\"color:inherit\">Guides</a></div>\n      <h3><a href=\"/blog/spotting-fake-reviews-and-invented-ratings-in-directories/\">Spotting fake reviews and invented ratings in directories</a></h3>\n      <p>Most directories score every site 9-point-something. Here is how to tell a real assessment from a formula.</p>\n      <a class=\"more\" href=\"/blog/spotting-fake-reviews-and-invented-ratings-in-directories/\">Read guide →</a>\n    </article><article class=\"post-card\">\n      <div class=\"tagline\"><a href=\"/blog/topic/safety/\" style=\"color:inherit\">Safety</a></div>\n      <h3><a href=\"/blog/how-to-tell-a-real-adult-site-from-a-malware-trap/\">How to tell a real adult site from a malware trap</a></h3>\n      <p>The five signals that separate a legitimate platform from a page that just wants your browser.</p>\n      <a class=\"more\" href=\"/blog/how-to-tell-a-real-adult-site-from-a-malware-trap/\">Read guide →</a>\n    </article></div>\n  </section>\n</article></main>\n<footer class=\"site-foot de-foot\">\n  <div class=\"de-foot-band\"><div class=\"container\">\n    <div class=\"de-foot-top\">\n      <a class=\"brand\" href=\"/\"><img class=\"brand-logo\" src=\"/assets/logo.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\"><span class=\"wordmark\"><b>Dark</b><span class=\"ero\">-Ero</span></span></a>\n      <p>An independent adult-site directory. Listings go straight to the site. Scores appear only after a real review.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"de-foot-icons\">\n      <a href=\"/contact/\" aria-label=\"Contact\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"